## 1. Ownership of Salary Review Process

a. The Hiring Manager is fully responsible for:
- initiating salary review requests in BambooHR;
- tracking when compensation changes are required;
- ensuring all changes are properly justified and documented.
b. Salary reviews are not automated and must always be initiated by the Hiring Manager.
c. The Hiring Manager is expected to:
- proactively monitor employee performance and compensation relevance;
- align proposed changes with HR before submission.
d. HR supports the process but does not initiate salary changes.

## 2. When to Initiate a Salary Review

a. Salary reviews may be initiated in the following cases:
- after successful completion of the probation period (as per offer terms);
- based on performance and contribution;
- in cases of role or responsibility changes;
- as part of structured review cycles (if applicable to the team).
b. The Hiring Manager is responsible for ensuring that offer-based commitments (e.g., postprobation increases) are fulfilled on time.

## 3. Review Preparation

a. Before submitting a request, the Hiring Manager:
- evaluates employee performance;
- reviews the current compensation level;
- ensures internal fairness within the team;
- aligns expectations with HR.
b. The Hiring Manager defines:
- new salary amount;
- effective date;
- justification for the change.

## 4. Creating a Compensation Change Request in BambooHR

a. The Hiring Manager opens the employee profile in BambooHR.
b. Selects:
- Request a Change → Compensation
c. Completes the required fields:
- Start Date — effective date of the new salary;
- Pay Rate — updated salary amount;
- Change Reason — appropriate reason (e.g., Salary Review, Probation Review).
d. Verifies that other fields remain unchanged unless adjustment is required.
e. Adds a comment including:
- performance summary;
- key achievements and impact;
- clear justification for the change.

# Onboarding and Adaptation Process

Audience
This document is intended for:
Employees – to understand onboarding stages, expectations, and feedback milestones;
Managers – to understand onboarding responsibilities, feedback requirements, and probation decisions;
HR – to ensure consistency, coordination, and compliance.

### 1. Vacancy Initiation

a. The Manager informs HR of the need to open a vacancy.
b. The Manager provides HR with key information:

- Job Description: responsibilities, requirements, candidate level;
- Expected Compensation: approximate salary range;
- Employment Conditions: full-time/part-time, contract type (GIG/FOP), preferred start date, etc

c. HR reviews the provided details carefully and may give feedback on:

- market alignment of the compensation;
- accuracy of the job description;
- clarifying questions on conditions.

